# ==============================================================================
# GPU & display
# ==============================================================================
# Kitchen-sink strategy: ship every common GPU driver in the live ISO so
# boot succeeds on AMD / Intel / NVIDIA hardware out of the box, then
# /usr/local/bin/cleanup-unused-drivers (a Calamares shellprocess that
# runs after install-gpu-drivers) removes the drivers that don't match
# the detected GPU vendor. Adds ~600 MB to the ISO; trades download size
# for "it just booted" on every machine.
#
# linux-headers is required for DKMS (nvidia-open-dkms below, also any
# Realtek Wi-Fi DKMS added later). Pruned post-install if no DKMS
# packages survive the cleanup pass.
linux-headers
mesa
vulkan-radeon
vulkan-intel
intel-media-driver
xf86-video-amdgpu

# NVIDIA drivers are NOT shipped in the live airootfs — install-gpu-drivers
# picks the right one at install time (nvidia-open for Turing+, nvidia-580xx-
# dkms for Maxwell–Volta, etc.) based on detected hardware. The live session
# falls back to nouveau on NVIDIA cards, which is fine for the installer UI.
#
# Why not pre-ship: nvidia-open-dkms's modinfo references ~107 MB of GSP
# firmware, which the kms initramfs hook auto-bundles. That ballooned
# initramfs-linux.img to 242 MB and Limine couldn't fit the boot bundle
# into a contiguous high-memory region on some UEFI memory maps ("High
# memory allocator: out of memory" panic on ~every other cold boot).

